KZ3 patch 2146: the product name in the settings folder and the settings files' comments comes from
PS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME (default "Project Helghast", so this port's behaviour is unchanged: same %APPDATA% folder, same
text in keybinds.ini and display.ini). Patches 2037, 2095, 2103 and 2121 hard-coded the name, so a second port built
from the same series wrote its settings into this port's folder under this port's name. Ported from the Ratchet &
Clank port, patch 6010 (same change; there it sits after 4028, here it is numbered before it, so the comment
"else %APPDATA%\Project Helghast" in cellPad.c, which patch 4028 quotes as context, is left as it is). A port sets the
name with -DPS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME="\"Name\"" on the runtime. Host test tools/smoke/test_product_name.sh.
Upstream candidate with the settings-folder patches (2037).

--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -434,7 +434,7 @@
     n = GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"APPDATA", appdata, 1024);
     if (n > 0 && n < 1000) {
         wchar_t dir[1024];
-        _snwprintf(dir, 1024, L"%ls\\Project Helghast", appdata); dir[1023] = 0;
+        _snwprintf(dir, 1024, L"%ls\\%hs", appdata, PS3RECOMP_PRODUCT_NAME); dir[1023] = 0;
         CreateDirectoryW(dir, NULL);                  /* exists already = fine */
         _snwprintf(s_kb_path, 1024, L"%ls\\keybinds.ini", dir); s_kb_path[1023] = 0;
         return;
--- a/libs/input/pad_keybinds.h
+++ b/libs/input/pad_keybinds.h
@@ -51,6 +51,13 @@
 
